:::writing{id="68423" variant="email" subject="Clarification on Income Tax Withholding and Digital Platform Taxation"}
Dear Hassam,

We hope this message finds you well. Thank you for sharing the additional commercial and operational details for Oxford Reading Buddy (ORB), Oxford My E-Mate, and Oxford Extend, together with your follow-up queries primarily relating to the withholding of income tax. We have carefully reviewed the supplementary information in conjunction with our earlier advice and the relevant provisions introduced through the Finance Act, 2025. Based on this review, we confirm that the additional facts do not alter the overall income-tax characterization of the digital platforms; rather, they further strengthen the conclusion that the receipts fall squarely within the scope of section 6A of the Income Tax Ordinance, 2001. Set out below is our consolidated understanding of the additional information and our detailed responses to your specific withholding-tax and related queries, aimed at providing clarity on both the legal position and its practical application.
